{% from "_base.html.j2" import head, foot %}{% from "_comparison.html.j2" import comparison %}{{ head(e.experiment ~ " — isbetter report") }}
<h1>{{ e.experiment }}</h1>
<p class="meta">isbetter {{ e.package_version }} &middot; seed {{ e.seed }} &middot; {{ e.created_at }}</p>

<h2>Plan</h2>
<pre>{{ plan_text }}</pre>

<h2>Sample-ratio check</h2>
{% if e.srm %}
<p><span class="badge {{ 'bad' if e.srm.flagged else 'good' }}">{{ "FAILED" if e.srm.flagged else "Passed" }}</span> {{ e.srm.rationale }}</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Arm</th><th class="num">Observed</th><th class="num">Expected</th><th class="num">Planned share</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for arm in e.srm.observed %}<tr><td>{{ arm }}</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(e.srm.observed[arm]) }}</td><td class="num">{{ "{:,.1f}".format(e.srm.expected[arm]) }}</td><td class="num">{{ "%.1f"|format(e.srm.expected_share[arm] * 100) }}%</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% if not e.srm.approx_ok %}<p class="warning"><em>Warning: an expected count is below 5, so the chi-square approximation is unreliable.</em></p>{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>Not applicable: paired and cross-validation designs have equal arm sizes by construction.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Decision</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Candidate</th><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for d in e.decisions %}<tr><td>{{ d.candidate }}</td><td><span class="badge {{ 'good' if d.ship else 'bad' }}">{{ "SHIP" if d.ship else "DO NOT SHIP" }}</span></td><td>{{ d.reason }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% for d in e.decisions %}
<h3>{{ d.candidate }} vs {{ baseline }}</h3>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Role</th><th>Result</th><th class="num">Effect</th><th>CI</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for c in d.checks %}<tr><td>{{ c.metric }}</td><td>{{ c.role }}</td><td>{{ c.status }}</td><td class="num">{{ fmt(c.oriented_estimate) }}</td><td>[{{ fmt(c.oriented_ci_low) }}, {{ fmt(c.oriented_ci_high) }}]</td><td>{{ c.detail }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% endfor %}
<p class="why">Effects are <strong>candidate &minus; baseline</strong>, oriented so positive means the
candidate wins. Success-metric intervals carry the multiplicity correction ({{ e.plan.correction }}
across all success hypotheses). Guardrail intervals are two-sided {{ "%.0f"|format((1 - 2 * e.plan.alpha) * 100) }}% intervals, i.e. a one-sided
test at the unadjusted &alpha; = {{ e.plan.alpha }}; a guardrail passes only if the lower limit is above minus its margin.</p>

<h2>Results by metric</h2>
{% for p, res in pairs %}
<h3>{{ p.metric }} ({{ p.role }})</h3>
{% if p.role == "guardrail" %}<p class="why"><em>Guardrail: the margin below is the non-inferiority margin, not an equivalence band; read the decision above rather than the verdict label.</em></p>{% endif %}
{% for c in res.comparisons %}{{ comparison(c, res, 4, label_text, tone, row, figure) }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
{{ foot() }}
